WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:09.920
Here we go again. It’s time to return to the&nbsp;
acid-filled containment chamber of SCP-682,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:15.840
more commonly known as the Hard to Destroy&nbsp;
Reptile. We’ve spoken about him and the ways&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:22.800
The SCP Foundation has attempted to destroy him&nbsp;
in a previous video. But as we said back then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:28.800
we really only scratched the surface of the huge&nbsp;
number of insane ways the Foundation has tried&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:32.640
to wipe this ornery lizard&nbsp;
off the face of the earth.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:38.160
Today, we’re filling in some of the cracks. Let’s&nbsp;
take a look at the secret test logs detailing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:49.040
the Foundation’s unsuccessful quest to finally&nbsp;
destroy SCP-682. If you’re a real SCP Expert,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:54.080
you’re likely to recognize some&nbsp;
familiar faces we meet along the way...

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:59.360
Esteemed Foundation Researcher Dr. Alto&nbsp;
Clef - famed for his somewhat unconventional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:04.800
personality - entered the test chamber to see&nbsp;
if he could intimidate the beast to death.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:12.240
This resulted in a long staring contest between&nbsp;
Dr. Clef and 682, towards the end of which, Dr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:18.400
Clef began to lose his nerve. He tried to leave&nbsp;
the room, only to find that the door was locked,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:22.480
causing him to swear loudly. Dr.&nbsp;
Clef, who always tries to find the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:28.720
most direct solution to his problems, blew up&nbsp;
the door with plastic explosives and ran off.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:34.320
Test failed.
Next came SCP-662,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:40.800
a silver hand bell that summons the supernaturally&nbsp;
helpful butler, Mr. Deeds. When Mr. Deeds was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:47.440
summoned, Foundation researchers asked him if&nbsp;
he could kill SCP-682. Deeds politely explained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:53.840
that he wouldn’t be capable of killing 682, it’s&nbsp;
just too strong. When asked if he could at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.840 --> 00:02:00.960
incapacitate 682, he replied that the best way to&nbsp;
do this would be to poison himself and allow 682&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:07.040
to eat his body. But this, he reminded, would&nbsp;
only be a temporary problem for the lizard.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:10.400
Test failed.
The Foundation brought in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:17.360
SCP-689, a terrifying soapstone statue of a&nbsp;
sitting skeleton that can kill you if you see it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:21.840
and then stop paying attention to&nbsp;
it. 682 first observed the statue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:28.720
and then the Foundation turned off the lights.&nbsp;
When they turned them back on, SCP-682 appeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:35.120
to be dead in a puddle of gray and black liquid.&nbsp;
D-Classes were sent in to confirm that 682 was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:41.360
actually dead, but it instead got up and killed&nbsp;
them. Researchers theorized that 682’s definition&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:48.400
of “life” is not quite the same as ours,&nbsp;
rendering 689’s death-related powers ineffective.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:49.280
Test failed.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:57.840
SCP-807 was next up to bat. This is an anomalous&nbsp;
salmon-colored ceramic dinner plate with the words&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:01.120
"Last Chance Diner" printed on the edges in white.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:06.320
Any food placed on it becomes irresistible by&nbsp;
any definition, but when the food is consumed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:11.680
it causes immediate cardiac arrest due to&nbsp;
the sudden clogging of the arteries with fat.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:17.280
Researchers made a meal known as the&nbsp;
“682 Special” - 10 kg of rotten meat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:23.680
and sharpened bone splinters, 10 L of&nbsp;
rancid mayonnaise, 1 L potassium cyanide,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:30.640
and 1 kg morphine hydrochloride, combined&nbsp;
into a solid mass and transmuted by 807.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:35.680
When 682 first consumed this&nbsp;
disgusting meal, it seemed to collapse.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:41.760
However, when D-Classes were sent in to see&nbsp;
whether 682 was truly out for the count,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:47.120
multiple holes opened in its body. These&nbsp;
holes fired out high-pressure jets of blood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:53.520
killing the nearby D-Classes and destroying&nbsp;
the containment cell. 682 was fine afterwards.

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:57.520
Test failed.
To kill 682, it seemed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:04.560
that the Foundation really needed to have God&nbsp;
on their side. So they tried to recruit SCP-343,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:10.320
also known as “God”, to help them destroy the&nbsp;
beast. However, when he entered the containment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:14.800
chamber, he somehow couldn’t even see the&nbsp;
beast. When researchers asked him whether&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:20.400
he could kill 682, God replied, “He's&nbsp;
not one of mine. Deal with him yourself."

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:21.200
Test failed.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:30.720
Next, the Foundation recruited SCP-524: A small&nbsp;
white rabbit that can eat literally anything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:36.800
including itself, without being harmed. The&nbsp;
rabbit was released into SCP-682’s chamber,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:42.880
at which point it approached 682 and began to&nbsp;
eat one of its legs. 682 roared in pain and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:49.200
scuttled up the wall, out of 524’s reach, where&nbsp;
it remained for a number of hours. At this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:55.120
SCP-524 seemed to become bored, and began eating&nbsp;
its way out of containment through a nearby wall.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:56.480
Test failed.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:01.040
Maybe the luck of the Irish was what the&nbsp;
Foundation needed to finally put this monster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:08.160
to rest. They recruited SCP-1933, a fat man&nbsp;
dressed as Santa Claus whose bodily fluids are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:13.680
entirely the alcoholic beverage known as&nbsp;
Irish Cream. However, if enough of this Irish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:20.000
cream is fed to something, all of their bodily&nbsp;
fluids will become Irish cream, killing them.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:28.240
The Foundation fed large quantities of this&nbsp;
Irish cream to SCP-682. At first, it appeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:36.720
intoxicated, a promising sign. However, it vomited&nbsp;
out a massive quantity of SCP-1933 bodily fluids,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:41.840
turning the walls of its cell into Irish cream&nbsp;
and allowing it to escape and wreak havoc.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:48.080
Test failed.
The Foundation recruited the help of SCP-2337,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:53.520
an intelligent corn crake known as Dr. Spanko,&nbsp;
with a voice so loud it can quite literally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:58.320
talk its victims to death if it speaks&nbsp;
to them for an extended period of time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:05.280
It was sent into SCP-682’s chamber to destroy&nbsp;
the beast, but 682 just told it to leave,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:10.720
and the talkative bird obliged - by blowing&nbsp;
away one of the chamber walls with a yell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:14.480
allowing SCP-682 to breach containment again.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:18.160
Test failed.

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:20.480
As you can probably sympathize with right now,&nbsp;
the Foundation researchers were starting to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:27.520
a little frustrated with their lack of progress.&nbsp;
They even pitched the possibility of sending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:34.720
SCP-682 into an alternate dimension, perhaps&nbsp;
into a stalemate against its alternate self.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:41.600
But this pitch was shot down by the O5 Council on&nbsp;
the grounds that it was way, way, way too risky.

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:47.200
Back to the drawing board. By which we mean,&nbsp;
they literally transformed SCP-682’s skin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:52.080
into a kind of drawing board.
SCP-2521 is an anomaly that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:56.960
manifests any time information about it&nbsp;
is recorded, and immediately grabs the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.960 --> 00:07:01.600
source of the information, wrapping it in&nbsp;
its tendrils and taking it away with it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:07.440
The Foundation sought to take advantage of this&nbsp;
by using a laser to cut this anomalous information&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:14.080
into SCP-682’s side. However, this didn’t&nbsp;
have the results that they were hoping for.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:18.960
SCP-2521 did turn up to take the&nbsp;
information, but it only took the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:25.600
skin on which the information was carved.&nbsp;
682 survived and quickly grew back its skin.

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:31.520
Test failed.
Researchers suggested tracking down SCP-169,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:38.160
an obscenely massive underwater creature known&nbsp;
as The Leviathan, and feeding 682 to the beast.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:44.800
However, this idea was immediately shot down&nbsp;
by the O5 Council. If 682 did what it did best:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:52.720
Surviving the attack and acting accordingly,&nbsp;
perhaps by growing to the size of SCP-169,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:58.880
it would likely trigger an XK-Class End of the&nbsp;
World Scenario. It simply was not worth the risk.&nbsp;

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:08.640
The Foundation released two specimens of SCP-939&nbsp;
into 682’s test chamber. These voice-imitating,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:13.040
amnesia-inducing monsters have&nbsp;
caused huge damage to human targets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:19.600
so maybe they had some hope against 682.&nbsp;
This hope turned out to be misplaced: Both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:27.360
specimens seemed extremely distressed by 682’s&nbsp;
presence and refused to engage. 682 did not have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:33.680
that same refusal. It charged in and brutally&nbsp;
killed both, before devouring their corpses.

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:38.080
Test failed.
In a very well-documented case, the adorable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:45.280
SCP-999 was introduced into 682’s test chamber.&nbsp;
The unassailable good vibes provided by 999,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:52.640
as well as an intense tickle fight, did actually&nbsp;
lead to the temporary incapacitation of SCP-682.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:59.040
However, the otherwise wholesome incident ended in&nbsp;
tragedy when 682 adapted to the good vibes and was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:04.400
able to release a kind of violent laughter&nbsp;
wave. This incapacitated much of the staff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:10.880
and allowed 682 to breach containment and go on&nbsp;
another killing spree, before being recontained.

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:13.120
Test, once again, failed.

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:16.480
One of the closest attempts the&nbsp;
Foundation ever had involved SCP-294,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:21.040
an anomalous coffee machine that can&nbsp;
produce any liquid typed into its keypad.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:27.840
Foundation researchers requested “SCP-682&nbsp;
Killer” from the machine, and were astounded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:37.440
at the results. During tests on SCP-682 tissue&nbsp;
samples, the liquid was capable of causing 682&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:43.280
tissue to decay and crumble. Tests on the living&nbsp;
creature were similarly promising. The acid in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:51.680
682’s tank was receded, and one liter of SCP-682&nbsp;
Killer was poured onto it, causing that portion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:59.440
of its flesh to immediately decay. When the acid&nbsp;
was returned, this portion dissolved instantly.

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:11.040
Scientists believe that if they could one day&nbsp;
get a large enough quantity of this liquid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:16.320
they might have a viable option.&nbsp;
But until then, the tests march on.

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:23.760
They introduced SCP-055, the self-keeping&nbsp;
secret, into the containment chamber of SCP-682.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:31.236
We don’t really know what happened, but seeing&nbsp;
as 682 isn’t dead, we now know that 055 can’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.236 --> 00:10:41.760
kill it. That and the fact it isn’t round&nbsp;
is pretty much all we know about SCP-055.

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:46.320
Test failed.

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:57.680
Next came SCP-082, also known as Fernand the&nbsp;
Cannibal. Fernand was first presented a piece&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.680 --> 00:11:02.800
of flesh from 682, but rather than eating&nbsp;
it, he inspected it and began to express&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:07.760
joy that his “friend” still lived. When&nbsp;
introduced into 682’s testing chamber,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:13.360
Fernand attempted to subdue the lizard&nbsp;
and use it as his steed. 682 expressed an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:18.560
intense hatred of both Fernand and the idea&nbsp;
of being Fernand’s steed, so the two of them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:24.560
engaged in combat. Mobile Task Forces were&nbsp;
eventually brought in to subdue both subjects.

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:28.080
In the debrief interview, both hinted&nbsp;
that the two of them shared history prior&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:31.680
to containment. 682 was&nbsp;
reluctant to talk about it.

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:35.600
Test failed.

00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:41.360
Researchers were becoming extremely frustrated&nbsp;
with SCP-682’s unwillingness to die,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:49.280
so they called in an SCP who responded to&nbsp;
reason much better: SCP-049, the Plague Doctor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.280 --> 00:11:55.840
This sinister surgeon can kill with a touch, and&nbsp;
the Foundation hoped that would extend to 682.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.400 --> 00:12:00.880
However, the result was a dud.&nbsp;
The Plague Doctor did touch 682,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:06.400
but it experienced no adverse effects, and&nbsp;
even swiped at the doctor. Upon leaving,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:13.440
049 reported feeling “emotionally&nbsp;
disturbed” by his encounter with SCP-682.

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:16.720
Yep, you guessed it: Test failed.

00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:21.200
If it gives you any indication of just how&nbsp;
desperate the researchers were at this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:26.480
Dr. Richard Graham pondered whether introducing&nbsp;
SCP-682 to a human with just as pessimistic and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:32.080
misanthropic feelings as itself would somehow&nbsp;
pacify it. They sent in a particularly nasty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:37.760
D-Class, and the two spoke. Fascinatingly,&nbsp;
682 didn’t attempt to harm this D-Class,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:42.080
they just shared their profane and bleak&nbsp;
sentiments about the human race with one another.

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:47.360
However, some of 682’s opinions were&nbsp;
a little too spicy for this D-Class.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:47.360 --> 00:12:51.280
After listening to the reptile speak&nbsp;
for twenty minutes, the D-Class fell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:56.480
into a catatonic state from the sheer&nbsp;
depression of it all. He died not long after.

00:12:56.480 --> 00:13:00.400
One anonymous researcher suggested&nbsp;
perhaps the worst idea of all:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:07.280
Letting SCP-682 out into the wild. Not even to&nbsp;
really terminate it, just to see what it does.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.280 --> 00:13:11.280
The anonymous scientist figured there would be&nbsp;
some merit in analyzing the creature’s behavior.

00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:26.080
As you can probably guess, this request&nbsp;
was shot down by the O5 Council.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:29.760
The note attached to the request by&nbsp;
one of its members summed it up best:

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:34.160
“I'll tell you what it'll do. It'll go out for&nbsp;
a nice stroll, murder a few innocent people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:39.520
go fishing, slaughter a few more innocent people,&nbsp;
start up a tech-company, eat a few more innocent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:45.280
people, go on a vacation to Florida, dismember a&nbsp;
few more innocent people! I swear, when I find out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:50.640
who wrote this, you can personally enter 682's&nbsp;
containment chamber to analyze him yourself!”

00:13:50.640 --> 00:14:02.000
Even this isn’t covering every single attempt to&nbsp;
terminate SCP-682, but all attempts have either&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:06.800
been failures or too risky or potentially&nbsp;
unviable to even try. Sadly, for the SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:13.840
Foundation and the human race, it’s likely we’ll&nbsp;
be dealing with SCP-682 for a long time to come.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:22.720
How do you think 682 could finally be killed?&nbsp;
Let us know down in the comments below!

00:14:22.720 --> 00:14:30.160
Now check out “SCP-682 - Ways The Foundation Tried&nbsp;
To Kill The Hard To Destroy Reptile” and “SCP-999&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:36.000
- The Tickle Monster” for more fascinating&nbsp;
facts about this lizard with anger issues.

